{
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "The immutable, informational owner-readiness projection.\n\nFixed literals make the boundary explicit: this summary never approves,\nauthorizes or executes anything, and it is not an authorization bearer.\nA READY plan observed here is a *fact about a fresh plan derivation*,\nnot a permission; the apply boundary re-derives everything under its\nown locks and expected hashes.",
  "properties": {
    "contract": {
      "const": "owner_readiness_summary_v1",
      "default": "owner_readiness_summary_v1",
      "title": "Contract",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "schema_version": {
      "default": "1.0.0",
      "pattern": "^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$",
      "title": "Schema Version",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "summary_id": {
      "description": "Semantic observed-core identity of this journey observation \u2014 NOT a unique identity of the complete projection (the Phase 7-C4-D contract decision). It is derived from the published base/target profile identities and byte hashes, the release manifest identity/content hash, the fresh activation plan id plus the full plan content hash (which transitively binds the whole plan payload, including the supplied project-config path spelling through the plan's config inventory), the activation-store status, the observed project-config byte hash and the derived journey state. It deliberately excludes the activation-store problems/guidance and the next-step hint text (including decision/exception/trust/evidence path spellings displayed there), so two observations that differ only in those presentation fields share one summary_id while differing in content_sha256. Equal summary_id means 'same semantic journey observation', never 'byte-identical summary'; exact-projection equality, and any deduplication or persistence key, must use content_sha256 (or the pair (summary_id, content_sha256) when semantic grouping plus an exact variant is needed).",
      "minLength": 1,
      "title": "Summary Id",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "base_profile_id": {
      "maxLength": 128,
      "minLength": 1,
      "title": "Base Profile Id",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "base_profile_sha256": {
      "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
      "title": "Base Profile Sha256",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "target_profile_id": {
